# Media policy (revised 2026-07-11, per central media-volume-storage rule):
# VITAL runtime media stays COMMITTED; BULK non-runtime media lives on Google Drive
# (gdrive:skeuo-ui/gen12-media/2026-07-11/, sha256-verified mirror) and is IGNORED here —
# see MEDIA-MANIFEST.md / media-manifest.json for repo-path <-> Drive-path <-> sha256.
# Evidence basis (grep of the committed player.html / player-pbr.html / dashboard12.html
# for actual runtime img/url()/fetch refs — TODO.md "Media policy revisit"):
#   COMMITTED (runtime-required): assets-*/paint.png (player background), assets-*/mask.png
#     (player compositing), assets-*_biref/ cut sprites (device/seek/vol/shuffle_*/extra-*),
#     assets-*_pbr/ maps loaded by player-pbr.html (basecolor/normal/roughness/metalness/
#     glass/btn-ids/emissive/art-mask/viz-mask/meta.json), and
#     assets-steam-porthole_biref/global-matte.png ONLY (dashboard12.html's embedded
#     explainer_anim.js hardcodes KNOB_SKIN="assets-steam-porthole" and loadImg's it).
#   ON DRIVE + IGNORED (no runtime refs anywhere): assets-*/joint-4k.png (paid Vertex roll,
#     also recoverable from git history commit 39d76200), assets-*_biref/global-matte.png
#     except steam-porthole ($0-recomputable via local BiRefNet BIREF_LOCAL=True),
#     assets-*_pbr/height.png.
assets-*/joint-4k.png
assets-*_biref/global-matte.png
!assets-steam-porthole_biref/global-matte.png
assets-*_pbr/height.png
assets-*/overlay.png
assets-*/blueprint.png
__pycache__/
.venv-biref/
review.json
pbrtest/pydeps/
assets-*/observe/*.png
assets-*/director/*.png
.director-drive-*.mjs

# inpaintbake/ (2026-07-12 inpaint bake-off): bulk generation scratch — inputs (crops/),
# raw model outputs (results/), and derived display thumbnails (web/) are all regenerable
# via build_crops.py + run_bakeoff.py + build_page.py against the committed erasegallery/
# source images and scoring JSON. The durable, LFS-tracked archival record (comparison
# strips) lives in docs/experiments/assets/2026-07-12-inpaint-bakeoff-*.jpg instead — same
# "bulk on disk, curated evidence in git" split as the rest of this policy.
inpaintbake/crops/
inpaintbake/results/
inpaintbake/web/
inpaintbake/.serve-url

# Same policy for the un-landed bake-off arms (editors/ = arm-3, arm4/ = arm-4): only the
# .py/.html/.json code + verdicts are durable; their generated PNG/JPG media stays local
# scratch, regenerable via each arm's own committed build_composites.py/build_page.py.
inpaintbake/editors/results/
inpaintbake/editors/web/
inpaintbake/editors/tight/
inpaintbake/arm4/results/
inpaintbake/arm4/web/
